{
  "summary": "Fix an assertion crash on startup during AssumeUTXO background sync when a node restarts with the snapshot block downloaded ahead of its ancestors. On startup, `LoadBlockIndex()` now adds the snapshot block to `m_blocks_unlinked` if its parent has no transaction count, and `PopulateBlockIndexCandidates()` skips registering it as a candidate tip until its ancestors are present.",
  "problem": "During AssumeUTXO background sync, blocks up to the snapshot block can be downloaded out of order from multiple peers, placing the snapshot block into storage before its parent. If the node restarts in this window, `LoadBlockIndex()` sets the hardcoded chain transaction count on the snapshot block without restoring it to `m_blocks_unlinked`, causing `PopulateBlockIndexCandidates()` to select it as a tip candidate and `FindMostWorkChain()` to crash on `HaveNumChainTxs()` when walking back to its unlinked parent. Once hit, the node crashes on every startup unless restarted with `-reindex` or `-reindex-chainstate`, which wipes the snapshot chainstate.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"The new step in feature_assumeutxo.py restarts the node after the snapshot block is submitted out of order, and fails on master. I also reproduced it over p2p with a test peer that withholds the snapshot block's parent.\"",
    "PR description: \"cyb3ralbert hit the same assertion while testing #36452 (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36452#issuecomment-6464524112)\""
  ],
